1
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:29,154
Our Father, who art in heaven,
hallowed be Thy name.

2
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:32,449
Thy kingdom come,
Thy will be done,

3
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:35,827
on earth
as it is in heaven.

4
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:38,705
Give us this day
our daily bread,

5
00:00:38,747 --> 00:00:40,999
and forgive us
our trespasses,

6
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:45,170
as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

7
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:48,381
And lead us
not into temptation,

8
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:51,384
but deliver us from evil.

9
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:54,888
For Thine is the kingdom,
the power...

10
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:59,267
and the glory
now and forever.

11
00:00:59,351 --> 00:01:01,269
- Amen.
- Amen.

12
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:07,025
Thank you, Father Macklepenny,

13
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:11,654
for coming all the way
across town to be our guest speaker.

14
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,782
When I raise my flashing sword...

15
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:18,328
and my hand
takes hold on judgment,

16
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:23,208
I will take vengeance
up on mine enemies.

17
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:27,170
And I will repay those
who haze me.

18
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:31,633
O Lord, raise me
to Thy right hand...

19
00:01:31,716 --> 00:01:34,052
and count me
among Thy saints.

20
00:01:39,724 --> 00:01:42,435
And I am reminded
on this holy day...

21
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:47,816
of the sad story
of Kitty Genovese.

22
00:01:50,527 --> 00:01:54,489
As you all may remember,

23
00:01:54,531 --> 00:01:57,617
a long time ago,
almost 30 years ago,

24
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:01,830
this poor soul
cried out for help...

25
00:02:01,913 --> 00:02:04,457
time and time again,

26
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:08,461
but no person
answer her calls.

27
00:02:10,213 --> 00:02:12,465
Though many saw,

28
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:15,468
no one so much
as called the police.

29
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:21,433
They all just watched as Kitty
was being stabbed to death...

30
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:25,061
in broad daylight.

31
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:29,774
They watched as
her assailant walked away.

32
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:36,489
Now, we must all fear
evil men.

33
00:02:38,408 --> 00:02:41,661
But there is
another kind of evil...

34
00:02:41,745 --> 00:02:44,414
which we must fear most,

35
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:50,295
and that is
the indifference...

36
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:53,673
of good men!

37
00:03:13,401 --> 00:03:16,529
I do believe the monsignor's
finally got the point.

38
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:18,531
Aye.

39
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,984
Hey, Connor!

40
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:05,203
What?

41
00:04:16,131 --> 00:04:18,508
Yeah!
Who's the master?

42
00:04:25,348 --> 00:04:27,308
You're gonna be
training her today.

43
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,936
Aye.

44
00:04:37,152 --> 00:04:40,405
- Basically, the rule of thumb here is--
- Wait. Rule of thumb?

45
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:51,666
In the early 1900s, it was legal
for men to beat their wives...

46
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:55,003
as long as they used a stick
no wider than their thumb.

47
00:05:01,593 --> 00:05:03,553
Can't do much damage
with that then, can we?

48
00:05:03,636 --> 00:05:05,555
Perhaps it should've been
the ""rule of wrist.''

49
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:12,937
I knew you two pricks
would give me problems.

50
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:15,648
Come on. It's St. Patty's Day.
It's all in good fun.

51
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:17,692
Ah, fuck you!
And fuck you too!

52
00:05:19,069 --> 00:05:21,821
We're sorry, all right?
Just-Just relax.

53
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:27,160
Oh, shit.

54
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:27,929
Hey, fuck-ass,
give me a beer.

55
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:42,569
Listen, boys, I've got
some very bad news.

56
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:46,698
I'm gonna have to
close down t-t-the bar.

57
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:51,745
The Russians are buying up buildings
all over the town, includin' this one.

58
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:54,080
Fuck! Ass!

59
00:06:54,164 --> 00:06:56,750
And they're not lettin' me
renew my lease.

60
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:59,669
- Let me talk to my boss.

61
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:03,548
- Maybe he can do something.
- What the fuck's your boss gonna do?

62
00:07:03,631 --> 00:07:06,468
Listen, fellas,
I don't want anyone to know.

63
00:07:06,509 --> 00:07:08,595
Soyou keep your traps shut!

64
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:13,641
You know what they say:
People in glass houses sink s-s-ships.

65
00:07:17,312 --> 00:07:20,482
Hey, Doc, I gotta buy you,
like, a proverb book or somethin'.

66
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:23,109
This mix-and-match shit
has gotta go.

67
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:24,569
- What?

68
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:26,946
A penny saved is worth
two in the bush, isn't it?

69
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:30,367
And don't cross the road
ifyou can't get out ofthe kitchen.

70
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:40,251
What's this, then?

71
00:07:40,335 --> 00:07:45,382
I am Ivan Checkov,
and you will be closing now.

72
00:07:51,346 --> 00:07:53,390
Checkov.

73
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:58,853
Well, this here's McCoy.
We find a Spock,
we've got us an away team.

74
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:04,484
Me in no mood for discussion.
You, you stay.

75
00:08:04,526 --> 00:08:07,320
The rest of you,
go now.

76
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:11,366
Why don't you make like a tree
and get the fuck out of here!

77
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:17,706
You know he's got
till the week's end, right?

78
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:20,166
You don't have to be
hard-asses, doya?

79
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:22,877
- It's St. Patty's Day.
Everyone's Irish tonight.
- Mmm.

80
00:08:22,961 --> 00:08:25,213
Why don't you just
pull up a stool
and have a drink with us?

81
00:08:25,296 --> 00:08:27,841
- This is no game! If you won't go,

82
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:30,510
we will make you go.

83
00:08:48,111 --> 00:08:51,322
So these two guys are kickin'
the shit out of each other, right?

84
00:08:51,406 --> 00:08:54,284
This guy picks up
an old kitchen sink or something...

85
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:56,661
and fuckin' crushes
this guy with it.

86
00:08:56,745 --> 00:08:59,873
It makes a big bang.

87
00:09:23,355 --> 00:09:26,608
Look at him. His spine's all crushed.
Had to be one big motherfucker.

88
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:30,737
Huge. Three, four hundred pounds.
Fuckin' huge.

89
00:09:30,779 --> 00:09:33,198
- That's pretty thin.
- Very thin.

90
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,955
Okay.
Allright, allright.

91
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:43,583
Say these two guys right here,
they don't even know
the fuckin' huge guy.

92
00:09:43,625 --> 00:09:46,753
They're just staggering home
from a bar still all fucked up
from St. Patty's last night.

93
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:49,506
They decide to take a shortcut
down through the alley.

94
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,800
Wrong fuckin' alley, huh?

95
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:54,177
'Cause this big motherfucker,
he's just waitin' for 'em, right?

96
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:57,972
And what could be more perfect
for a strong-arm robbery?
Two drunk guys all bandaged up.

97
00:09:58,056 --> 00:10:00,558
They're already injured,
for Christ's sakes. Lookat 'em.

98
00:10:00,642 --> 00:10:04,020
These guys are stumblin'
through the alley.
 Too-ra-loo-ra-loo-la

99
00:10:04,104 --> 00:10:06,481
This guy takes a blunt object,
fuckin'-- Waah!

100
00:10:06,523 --> 00:10:09,818
Hits the guy with the bandages
around his head, right?
Why? 'Cause he's smart.

101
00:10:09,901 --> 00:10:13,113
He knows the guy with
the band age around his ass,
he ain't goin' nowhere.

102
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:15,824
He's goin' fuckin' nowhere!

103
00:10:15,907 --> 00:10:18,827
Where are you goin'?
Nowhere! That's right.

104
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:23,915
He ain't done yet.
He comes over and jumps
on this guy's back...

105
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:25,917
and crushes him to death.

106
00:10:27,502 --> 00:10:29,754
I feel something big here.

107
00:10:29,838 --> 00:10:32,007
I wouldn't be surprised to see
a lot of these turnin' up.

108
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:34,009
Brilliant!

109
00:10:34,092 --> 00:10:37,220
So now we got
a huge guy theory...

110
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:39,764
and a serial crusher theory.

111
00:10:39,848 --> 00:10:41,933
Top notch.

112
00:10:42,017 --> 00:10:44,269
- What's your name?
- Detective Greenly.

113
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:48,523
- Who the fuck are you?
- That's who the fuck I am.

114
00:10:48,606 --> 00:10:52,027
Listen, I gotta do this
by the numbers.

115
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:54,863
I.D. just came back
on these guys.

116
00:10:54,946 --> 00:10:57,115
They got connections
with the Russian mob.

117
00:10:57,198 --> 00:10:59,993
That makes it
a federal matter.

118
00:11:00,035 --> 00:11:04,539
And Agent Smecker here
is heading up the investigation
with our full cooperation.

119
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:07,834
- Why don'tyou get me a cup of coffee?
- Who the hell is this?

120
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:10,003
- A cafe latte, twist of lemon,
- What the fuck--

121
00:11:10,045 --> 00:11:13,381
- Chief, what the fuck is this?
- Sweet 'N Low.

122
00:13:30,727 --> 00:13:32,812
- Mitchell, Langley!

123
00:13:32,854 --> 00:13:35,899
- Yes, sir.
- Find the manager of this building.

124
00:13:35,982 --> 00:13:38,902
See if he's had any complaints
of water coming down...

125
00:13:38,985 --> 00:13:41,154
in any of the apartments
starting just this morning.

126
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,907
Langley, you take that building.
Same thing.

127
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,577
Chaffey! Newman!

128
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,830
- Yes, sir.
- Look in the trash around their hands.

129
00:13:50,914 --> 00:13:53,875
See if you can fnd me
two bullet casings,

130
00:13:53,917 --> 00:13:55,877
fifty-caliber
if my eyes serve me right.

131
00:13:57,504 --> 00:14:00,840
Newman,
rip through this shit.

132
00:14:00,882 --> 00:14:03,301
If this was a sink,

133
00:14:03,385 --> 00:14:05,303
find me some metal parts.

134
00:14:05,387 --> 00:14:08,890
Give me a drain cover,
faucet or something.

135
00:14:11,101 --> 00:14:13,061
Got it right here.
It's a 50-cal.

136
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:16,147
Chief, can you get
ballistics down here...

137
00:14:16,231 --> 00:14:18,900
and tell 'em they have to dig
a 50-caliber slug...

138
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:21,903
out of a brickwall
and locate another that's been
fred through a Dumpster?

139
00:14:21,945 --> 00:14:23,905
We have the best
ballistics guy in the world.

140
00:14:23,947 --> 00:14:26,658
- I can have him here in ten minutes.
- How did you know that?

141
00:14:26,741 --> 00:14:28,743
Liquid paraffn.

142
00:14:28,827 --> 00:14:31,121
Came up positive.

143
00:14:31,204 --> 00:14:33,540
And bullet holes
are usually a big clue.

144
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:35,875
Nobody reported
any gunshots.

145
00:14:35,917 --> 00:14:39,379
This is an Irish neighborhood.
I'm surprised you even got a phone call.

146
00:14:39,462 --> 00:14:42,215
You know, I can't find
these condone, sir.

147
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:44,259
Look under the body.

148
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:49,848
Oh, yeah, there it is.

149
00:14:51,975 --> 00:14:54,185
You guys ready for this?

150
00:14:54,269 --> 00:14:57,522
This was no
gangland assassination.

151
00:14:57,605 --> 00:15:00,233
Though creative,
it was way too sloppy.

152
00:15:00,275 --> 00:15:03,611
Something went wrong here.
This has ""personal'' written all over it.

153
00:15:03,695 --> 00:15:07,032
Agent Smecker.
Yeah, this is all illegal loft housing.

154
00:15:07,115 --> 00:15:09,909
There's no manager on
the premises, but they found
a lady on the fourth floor...

155
00:15:09,951 --> 00:15:12,162
who said she had water dripping
down on her whole place.

156
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:14,414
- It started just this morning.
- Fourth floor, huh?

157
00:15:14,497 --> 00:15:16,458
Mm-hmm.

158
00:15:17,709 --> 00:15:19,627
Then we're headin'
to the fifth.

159
00:15:19,711 --> 00:15:22,756
Come on. Let's get out of here.
You're reachin; man.

160
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:25,300
- It's a theory.
- I don't know. No way.

161
00:15:25,383 --> 00:15:28,303
You know how big a guy's
gotta be to do that? Fuckin' huge.

162
00:15:28,345 --> 00:15:32,599
Oh, really? I might just be
wantin' a bagel with my coffee.

163
00:15:39,314 --> 00:15:41,316
I ain't gettin' him
no fuckin' bagel.

164
00:15:50,367 --> 00:15:52,619
We'll start the ass kissing
with you.

165
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:59,501
Agent Smecker.
Agent--

166
00:15:59,542 --> 00:16:01,419
Listen, I know this neighborhood
pretty good.

167
00:16:01,503 --> 00:16:03,421
There's a bar down the block
named McGinty's.

168
00:16:03,505 --> 00:16:06,132
- It stands a good chance
they were there last night.
- Good work, Mitchell.

169
00:16:06,216 --> 00:16:08,802
I'll check it out myself.

170
00:16:08,843 --> 00:16:11,638
Lookat the ceiling.
Sensey our touch alone.

171
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,765
Wait until you feel me move.
Ooh.

172
00:16:13,848 --> 00:16:16,476
So quick you couldn't
even feel it go, could you?

173
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:19,604
Let's try it again.
Try it again. Look at the ceiling.

174
00:16:19,688 --> 00:16:21,606
It's Doc.

175
00:16:23,942 --> 00:16:27,612
- Thanks for comin', Doc.
- Jesus Christ!

176
00:16:27,696 --> 00:16:31,032
What the fuck happened?
Are-Are you b-b-boys all right?

177
00:16:31,116 --> 00:16:34,536
- We're alive.
- An F.B.I. agent came by the bar...

178
00:16:34,577 --> 00:16:36,538
and he left me
his c-c-ca--

179
00:16:36,579 --> 00:16:40,041
He left me his c-c--
Oh, he fuckin' gave me this.
Fuck!

180
00:16:40,125 --> 00:16:42,460
- Ass! What are you gonna do?

181
00:16:42,544 --> 00:16:45,005
We oughta turn ourselves in,
tell him it was self-defense.

182
00:16:45,088 --> 00:16:46,965
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's what he said.

183
00:16:47,048 --> 00:16:49,300
- How the fuck's he know that?
We haven't spoken to anyone.
- D-D-Don't know.

184
00:16:49,384 --> 00:16:52,012
He d-d-didn't say.

185
00:16:52,053 --> 00:16:54,639
All right. Listen, Doc,
we need you to do us a favor.

186
00:16:54,723 --> 00:16:57,350
- A-A-Anything.
-Just hold on to this for us.

187
00:16:57,392 --> 00:16:59,519
- We're gonna come back for it
when we get out.
- Right.

188
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,479
Fuck! Ass!

189
00:17:03,732 --> 00:17:07,402
None of that cursing
was directed at you.
He's-- He's a bit--

190
00:17:11,406 --> 00:17:13,366
First of all,

191
00:17:13,408 --> 00:17:16,536
I'd like to thank
which ever one of you...

192
00:17:16,578 --> 00:17:19,748
doughnut-munching,
barrel-assed,

193
00:17:19,831 --> 00:17:23,543
pud-pulling sissies
leaked this to the press.

194
00:17:24,794 --> 00:17:26,755
That's just
what we need now--

195
00:17:26,838 --> 00:17:28,882
some sensational story
in the papers...

196
00:17:28,923 --> 00:17:33,887
making these boys out to be
superheroes triumphing over evil.

197
00:17:33,970 --> 00:17:36,848
Let me squash
the rumors now.

198
00:17:36,931 --> 00:17:39,559
These two are not heroes.

199
00:17:41,269 --> 00:17:43,605
They're just
two ordinary men...

200
00:17:43,688 --> 00:17:47,400
who were put in
an extraordinary situation,

201
00:17:47,484 --> 00:17:49,861
and they just happened
to come out on top.

202
00:17:49,944 --> 00:17:53,907
Yes, nothing from our
far-reaching computer system...

203
00:17:53,948 --> 00:17:55,909
has turned up diddly
on these two.

204
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:58,370
All we know is what
we found out from the neighbors.

205
00:17:58,453 --> 00:18:00,372
And the general consensus is,

206
00:18:03,124 --> 00:18:05,043
they're angels.

207
00:18:07,796 --> 00:18:10,590
But angels don't kill.

208
00:18:10,632 --> 00:18:13,301
And we got
two bodies in the morgue...

209
00:18:13,385 --> 00:18:15,762
that look like they've been
serial-crushed...

210
00:18:15,804 --> 00:18:19,557
by some huge, friggin' guy.

211
00:18:19,641 --> 00:18:22,602
Are we considering these guys
armed and dangerous?

212
00:18:22,644 --> 00:18:24,646
Well, not armed.

213
00:18:24,688 --> 00:18:28,274
If they had guns,
they would've used them.
But dangerous? Very.

214
00:18:28,316 --> 00:18:30,276
Now, what makes you think
they're dangerous?

215
00:18:30,318 --> 00:18:32,821
- Maybe they're just
protectin' each other.

216
00:18:37,492 --> 00:18:40,995
Hey, look, I-I-I'm not sayin'
one way or the other.

217
00:18:41,079 --> 00:18:45,166
Just be careful and go
by the protocol on this.

218
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:48,628
It's grunt police work
that's gonna bring this one in.

219
00:18:48,670 --> 00:18:51,464
These guys are
miles away by now.

220
00:18:51,506 --> 00:18:54,801
But if you wanna beat your head
against the wall, then
here's what you're lookin'for.

221
00:18:54,843 --> 00:18:57,137
They're scared, like
two little bunny rabbits.

222
00:18:57,220 --> 00:19:00,140
Anything in a uniform
or flashing blue lights
is gonna spook 'em.

223
00:19:00,181 --> 00:19:04,185
Okay? So the only thing we can do
is put a potato on a string...

224
00:19:04,269 --> 00:19:06,187
and drag it through
South Boston.

225
00:19:06,271 --> 00:19:08,815
- Thanks for comin' out.

226
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:11,609
You'd probably have
better luckwith a beer.

227
00:19:13,028 --> 00:19:14,779
You would.

228
00:19:14,863 --> 00:19:17,699
- Oh, fuck.
- Hey, Greenly.

229
00:19:17,782 --> 00:19:20,827
Onion bagel, cream cheese.

230
00:19:33,131 --> 00:19:37,177
This conversation
is going to be recorded.

231
00:19:37,218 --> 00:19:39,512
Just answer to
the best of your knowledge.

232
00:19:39,554 --> 00:19:42,057
Excuse me, sir.
Please.

233
00:19:53,735 --> 00:19:56,196
Okay, we're ready.

